From 52596aea6a35e9178fe5d9c114aed956cfbeeb1c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vonic <phanquochoipt@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 19:06:57 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(plugin): cred-concurrency session affinity

The cred-concurrency plugin handles every pick whose candidates carry a
concurrency limit, which on this deployment is all of them. Because the host
only calls SessionAffinitySelector when the plugin declines, routing
.session-affinity never applied to real traffic: one conversation spread
across up to 13 antigravity accounts and cache_read fell to ~20% instead of
~88% for single-account sessions.

Pin each session to the credential that served it first, keyed by
provider+session+model and expired by session_affinity_ttl (default 1h).
Subagents inherit the parent pin via X-Parent-Session-Id and the ":agent:"
session suffix, mirroring session-affinity-subagents.

Pins are only created in the top priority tier and survive transient
busy-ness, so a session returns to its preferred credential instead of
sticking to a paid fallback for the whole TTL.
---
 examples/plugin/cred-concurrency/go/main.go   | 189 +++++++++++++++--
 .../plugin/cred-concurrency/go/main_test.go   | 190 ++++++++++++++++++
